hi,

I've released our current version of the transparent proxy patches in
patch-o-matic format.  The patch generally works well, the previous version
(#13) has been used in production for months, the latest version (#14) fixes
some conntrack collision problems and has been working for somewhat more
than a day.

Please include it in patch-o-matic/extra.

Parts of the patch are general changes useful for things other than tproxy.
Shall I submit those individually?

These other changes are:

netfilter specific:
-------------------
* an ICMP translation problem fix (already applied)
* nf_sock_release call, which makes it possible to do netfilter specific
  processing when a socket is closed (e.g. remove state associated to
  sockets)
* publish the functions manip_pkt (renamed to ip_nat_manip_pkt) and
  ip_nat_update_hashes (new function which updates the NAT hashes)
* new argument to ip_nat_setup_info() named flags, which makes it possible
  to bypass NAT helpers completely
* new field in ip_conntrack (placed in a way that struct ip_conntrack does
  not grow) named 'flags', which is currently used to "mark" connections as
  one initiated by a transparent proxy (IP_CTF_TPROXY)

core networking stuff:
----------------------
* IP_RECVORIGADDRS socket option, which patches the core network stack to
  support atomic destination address retrieval for UDP packets (IP_ORIGADDRS
  auxilary message)

